{"code": "AED16D", "name": "CHILD DEVELOPMENT IN EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION", "academic_units": 3, "exam_schedule": NaN, "common_information": "TUT^T^FRI^0930-1220^NIE,TR207^", "description": "This course conceptualizes children's development from birth to 8 years through the critical review of and reflection on various developmental theories, models, approaches and scholarly works. It will benefit participants working with young children in an early childhood context. 
